Lock Partially Despatched status, add Add Additional Shipping, fix packing
double-display (v0.146)

Three part-despatch issues Dan raised, all tied together:

1. The "(set automatically)" label on the Status dropdown was just the tip
   of a bigger problem: Partially Despatched could still be hand-picked
   away via that dropdown (e.g. "Awaiting Despatch"), which silently
   overwrote the order's real despatch state and was the only way users had
   found to re-release a short-shipped line for picking. It's now locked
   exactly like Invoice Pending/Completed - OrderService.update() rejects
   any manual status change away from it. The label itself is gone for all
   three locked statuses; the dropdown's disabled "Locked" message explains
   why instead.

   Partially Despatched now resolves only two ways:
     - Amending the order's line quantities down to match what's already
       despatched (or quantityDespatched up to match) closes it out
       automatically, onto Invoice Pending/Completed exactly like a real
       despatch would - no manual status flip needed any more. Reducing a
       quantity below what's already despatched is now rejected outright
       (use Reverse to Despatch / an RMA instead).
     - The new "Add Additional Shipping" button (2).

2. "Add Additional Shipping" - a new button on the order screen, shown only
   while Partially Despatched. Releases whatever's still outstanding
   straight back onto the picking queue (pickingStatus -> IN_PROGRESS, so
   it reappears on the handheld) without changing the order's status at
   all - stays Partially Despatched until the next despatch resolves it.
   Uses whatever courier/service is currently set in the existing Shipping
   section for this next delivery specifically - archiveCurrentShipment()
   (already used when reopening a fully-locked order) banks the previous
   leg's booking into Shipment history and clears the order's own dpd*/
   apc* identifiers first, so the next despatch books a genuinely new
   shipment rather than reusing the old one. Each Delivery row already
   snapshots its own courier at despatch time, so per-delivery courier
   history was mostly already there - this just makes it actually settable
   per shipment, which Orderwise couldn't do (it stuck to the order's
   original service for every shipment).

3. Packing was showing an already-despatched item alongside a newly-picked
   one whenever an order got a second, separate despatch (e.g. after Add
   Additional Shipping) - a genuine data-model gap, not a display bug:
   Carton had no idea which despatch it belonged to. Added a nullable
   delivery_id on cartons; DespatchService.confirmDespatch now tags every
   carton used in that despatch with the Delivery row it just created.
   PackingService/SerialPackingService's packing views now exclude any
   carton (and its lines/items) already tied to a Delivery, so a shipped
   item disappears from packing permanently once it's gone out.

Migration: V57__cartons_delivery_link.sql.

